# Bots and AI

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2 Vertical slice
Dependencies: `03_PLAYER_CAMERA_INPUT.todo`, `04_TERRITORY_PAINTING.todo`, `06_MATCH_FLOW_SCORING.todo`

## Purpose

Provide a fair, seedable opponent that demonstrates the game loop without hidden stat advantages.

On 2026-09-10 the developer replaced the parked stationary test-bot proposal with two mobile, competitive
bots: one fixed Ice and one fixed Fire, plus the human. They must fight enemies and pursue territory victory.
This explicitly authorizes bot integration before the outstanding hands-on approval of Match Flow.
The 16:37 IST follow-up asks bots to primarily target each other while retaining the human as a valid enemy.

## Tasks

- [x] Replace the stationary proposal with two mobile fixed-team opponents using the shared player silhouette,
  team-colored heads, real pooled projectiles, and territory-seeking behavior.
- [x] Define bot intent interface shared with human input.
- [x] Implement valid movement target selection.
- [x] Implement route painting behavior.
- [x] Implement contested-territory selection.
- [x] Implement basic opponent awareness.
- [x] Prefer eligible bot opponents with a bounded distance bias; preserve human targeting and win priorities.
- [x] Implement spray resource awareness for the existing firing interval and finite projectile pool.
- [x] Implement active-arena awareness.
- [x] Implement stuck detection and recovery.
- [x] Inject deterministic random source.
- [x] Add debug state overlay.
- [x] Add full-match bot test.
- [x] Record first bot profile tuning.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Bot uses the same movement, spray, and status rules as a human.
- [x] Fixed seed reproduces decisions for identical observations; Unity physics is not claimed bitwise deterministic.
- [x] Bots complete ten matches, ending inside the safe boundary, without permanent stuck states.
- [x] Bot does not spray continuously when recovery is required.
- [x] Difficulty does not use hidden movement or paint multipliers.
- [x] The bot with two enemies primarily chooses the other bot across ten live rounds; both-team scene
  checks and policy tests cover preference, human fallback, and preserved eligibility.
- [ ] Developer approves mobile behavior, combat readability, and complete match play.

## Completion evidence

2026-09-10 initial full baseline: 180 EditMode and 44 PlayMode tests passed.
The targeting follow-up passed all 69 policy cases and 9 competitive-bot PlayMode tests, including ten
live-physics, accelerated 120-second rounds. Fire chose the other bot for 218 engagements versus 52 for
the idle human (about 81%); the latest ten rounds used one Ice hard stuck recovery and all completed.
Horizontal-only progress tracking prevents vertical bouncing from hiding a stalled route.
Both factions won rounds. Other tests cover hostile-human targeting for either player team, friendly-fire
rejection, recoil protection, navigation around walls, unreachable surfaces, cleanup, UI bounds, and rematch.

Windows development build succeeded. The built three-player arena initialized with Direct3D 11 and no
runtime/shader error; the owned smoke process was stopped. This is startup evidence, not a human playtest
or minimum-spec FPS measurement.

Configuration: `EntropyTag/Assets/EntropyTag/Settings/Tuning/FirstSliceBots.asset`.
Documentation: `docs/16_COMPETITIVE_BOTS.md`.
Logs/results: ignored `EntropyTag/TestResults/` and `EntropyTag/Builds/Windows-development.log`.
Changes remain uncommitted with TODO 06 pending review. Canonical `.agent-context` remains read-only because
the current Context Mesh registry does not designate this base; session artifacts preserve the handoff.

